direct-once-bare
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: a `lazy val` whose rhs RUNS an operation by do-notation
  (`lazy val x = { Writer("abc"); 3 }`) but carries no explicit mark
  compiled as an EAGER bind: the direct-once rule keyed on hasMark,
  and a bare runnable statement is not a mark syntactically. Key on
  the compiled rhs instead — Out.Eff is the by-need case, Out.Pure
  stays a plain lazy val. One test that fails first.
files: src/main/scala/Direct.scala, src/test/scala/TestDirectOnce.scala, CHANGELOG.md
